WHAT THIS ROUND ESTABLISHES, which is not what it set out to establish:
  1. The zeros of F are NOT a uniform ladder when the weights decay.  Gaps run
     0.17-0.73 in units of pi/k, not 1.  The evenly spaced ladder theta_n = n pi/k
     is a CONSTANT-WEIGHT phenomenon (Theorem 2(e)), not a general one -- and the
     'doubled ladder' fingerprint must be stated with that scope in the note.
  2. The proposed instrument t* does not exist: |G_k| is already far above the
     threshold at t = 0 (it is essentially Gamma_k/2), so there is no first crossing
     from below.  The zero is produced by the PHASE turning, not by the envelope
     growing -- which also means the quantisation story was the wrong picture.
  3. Therefore the s = 1 constant remains UNSETTLED, and the two shapes registered
     at r206 stand as: shape B (lambda -> s-1/2) refuted; shape A (lambda -> s)
     consistent but not monotone, |lambda-s| = 0.02 to 0.16 at the largest k.

done.
